node.doctext:
Hello Monks,
<p>In Perl v5.10.1 I did not declare utf8 for require scripts, but in Perl v5.16.3 it is necessary.</p>
<p>What is another solution, do not change a lot of require scripts?</p>
<p>Now my index.pl script looks like this:</p>
<pre>
#!/usr/bin/perl
use CGI::Carp qw(warningsToBrowser fatalsToBrowser);
use utf8;
use CGI qw/:standard -utf8 -nosticky/;
use open qw/:utf8/;
binmode(STDOUT, ":utf8");
print header(-type => 'text/html',-charset => 'UTF-8');
print "one &#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085;\n";
require "index_req.pl";
print @select;
</pre>

index_req.pl
<pre>
#!/usr/bin/perl
@select = qw(one &#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085;);
1;
</pre>

output:
<blockquote>one &#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085; one????????</blockquote>

if I add utf8 in index_req.pl
<pre>
#!/usr/bin/perl
use utf8;
@select = qw(one &#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085;);
1;
</pre>

then output is good:
<blockquote>one &#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085; one&#1086;&#1076;&#1080;&#1085;</blockquote>
